{
  "company_name": "ReservoirSight Analytics",
  "industry": "Oil & Gas Upstream",
  "use_case": "Reservoir management and production optimization",
  "space_title": "ReservoirSight Analytics - Reservoir Management 🛢️",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Oil & Gas Upstream\n\n**Use case:** Reservoir Management & Production Optimization\n\nReservoirSight Analytics — subsurface and production analytics for 20 reservoirs spanning the Permian (Wolfcamp, Bone Spring, Spraberry), Eagle Ford, Williston (Bakken/Three Forks), Appalachian (Marcellus/Utica), Haynesville, DJ Basin (Niobrara), and Anadarko. Reservoir Engineers use this space day-to-day for decline-curve and water-cut surveillance; the Asset Manager and VP of Reserves use it to defend EUR, recovery factor, breakeven price, and infill-drilling capital allocation in monthly business reviews.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Oil rate (BOPD) and gas rate (MCF/day) — primary production volumes\n- Water cut % — sweep efficiency; >50% signals watered-out wells, >75% near-economic-limit\n- GOR (gas-oil ratio, SCF/BBL) — reservoir energy/phase indicator\n- Recovery factor % — shale typically 5-12%, conventional 25-50%\n- Annual decline rate % — shale wells often 30-50% Y1, 12-20% in later years\n- Cumulative oil (BBL) and estimated ultimate recovery (EUR)\n- OPEX per BOE — onshore US benchmark ~$8-15/BOE\n- Breakeven price (USD/BBL) — Permian Tier-1 ~$35-45, marginal acreage $55+\n\n**Data sources**\n- `production_readings` — daily oil/gas/water rates, pressure, temperature, lift method per reservoir\n- `reservoir_snapshots` — monthly cumulative oil, EUR, recovery factor, decline rate, water cut per reservoir\n- `reservoir_kpi_monthly` — monthly OPEX/BOE, breakeven price, monthly oil/gas volumes per reservoir",
  "schema_basename": "og_upstream_reservoir",
  "tables": [
    {
