  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Reservoir Management for an upstream operator with 20 reservoirs across the Permian (Wolfcamp, Bone Spring, Spraberry, San Andres), Eagle Ford (incl. Austin Chalk), Williston (Bakken, Three Forks), Appalachian (Marcellus, Utica), Haynesville (Haynesville, Bossier), DJ (Niobrara), and Anadarko (Woodford, Springer). Stakeholders include the Reservoir Engineer (rates, pressure, water cut, decline), Asset Manager (recovery factor, EUR, OPEX/BOE), and CFO/VP Reserves (breakeven price, capital allocation across basins).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Oil rate = oil_bpd (barrels per day); gas rate = gas_mcfpd; water rate = water_bpd.\n- Water cut % = water_cut_pct on reservoir_snapshots (or water_bpd/(oil_bpd+water_bpd) on production_readings). >50% watered-out, >75% near economic limit.\n- GOR (SCF/BBL) = gas_mcfpd*1000 / oil_bpd; rising GOR can indicate gas breakthrough.\n- Reservoir pressure = reservoir_pressure_psi; declining pressure drives lift method changes.\n- Recovery factor = recovery_factor_pct; shale 5-12%, conventional 25-50%.\n- Decline rate = decline_rate_pct (annual); shale wells often 30-50% Y1.\n- Cumulative oil = cumulative_oil_bbl; EUR = estimated_eur_bbl (BBL ultimately recoverable).\n- OPEX/BOE = opex_per_boe (USD); onshore US benchmark $8-15.\n- Breakeven = breakeven_price_usd (USD/BBL); Tier-1 Permian ~$35-45.\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - production_readings_metrics (source: production_readings) — dims: reading_date, reservoir_id, formation, basin, lift_method; measures: avg_oil_bpd, avg_gas_mcfpd, avg_water_bpd, avg_reservoir_pressure, total_bottomhole_temp_f, max_oil_bpd.\n  - reservoir_snapshots_metrics (source: reservoir_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_date, reservoir_id, formation, basin; measures: avg_recovery_factor, avg_decline_rate, avg_water_cut, total_cumulative_oil, total_estimated_eur_bbl, max_cumulative_oil_bbl.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. reservoir_name, opex_per_boe, breakeven_price_usd, monthly_oil_bbl, decline_rate_pct).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Top 10 reservoirs by average oil rate (BOPD) over the last 90 days.",
    "Show the monthly trend in average water cut and decline rate by basin for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which reservoirs have water cut above 60% and what is their cumulative oil and recovery factor?",
    "What is the average OPEX per BOE and breakeven price by basin and formation this year?",
    "Top 10 reservoirs by estimated ultimate recovery (EUR) — and how does that compare to cumulative oil produced?",
    "How has reservoir pressure trended month over month for Permian Basin wells?",
    "Which formations have the steepest annual decline rates, and what is their monthly oil volume?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "How has average oil barrels per day trended by month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(avg_oil_bpd) AS avg_oil_bpd",
        "FROM {fqn}.production_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average gas thousand cubic feet per day trended by month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(avg_gas_mcfpd) AS avg_gas_mcfpd",
        "FROM {fqn}.production_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total estimated ultimate recovery barrels trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(total_estimated_eur_bbl) AS total_estimated_eur_bbl",
        "FROM {fqn}.reservoir_snapshots_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Which reservoirs have the best average oil barrels per day?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reservoir_name, AVG(oil_bpd) AS avg_metric",
        "FROM {fqn}.production_readings",
        "GROUP BY reservoir_name",
        "ORDER BY avg_metric DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total cumulative oil barrels trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(cumulative_oil_bbl) AS total_cumulative_oil_bbl",
        "FROM {fqn}.reservoir_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does average recovery factor compare across basins?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT basin, AVG(recovery_factor_pct) AS avg_recovery_factor",
        "FROM {fqn}.reservoir_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY basin",
        "ORDER BY avg_recovery_factor DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average reservoir pressure changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(avg_reservoir_pressure) AS avg_reservoir_pressure",
        "FROM {fqn}.production_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
